IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-helpers`
IMPORT `oa1-part1-payment`

-- Tests of oa1-part1-payment. Every expected value is worked by hand from the text of ss 8 to 9.3 (lines 189-225).

§ `s 8(1): the earlier effective date`

-- Received January 15, 2026, approved February 10, 2026: approved after the last day (January 31) of the month received.
-- An earlier day not prior to January 15 and before the day of approval is allowed.
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 9)
-- Prior to the day received: not allowed. Not before the day of approval: not an earlier day.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 14))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10))
-- Approved on the last day of the month received is not "after the last day of the month".
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(1): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 20))

§ `s 8(2): the exception for a person who applied after sixty-five`

-- Born March 1, 1950 (65 on March 1, 2015); received June 15, 2026. One year before the day received is June 15, 2025, later than the 65th birthday: the earliest is June 15, 2025.
#ASSERT `s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14))
-- Not before the day received itself: the earlier day must be before it.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15))
-- Born January 10, 1961 (65 on January 10, 2026): the 65th birthday is later than a year before June 15, 2026 (June 15, 2025), so it is the earliest: January 10, 2026 is allowed, January 9 is not.
#ASSERT `s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1961 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1961 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 9))
-- Born March 1, 1962 (65 on March 1, 2027) had not attained 65 before the day received: the exception does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(2): the approval may be effective as of the earlier day` (YearMonthDay 1962 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
-- The later of two dates.
#ASSERT `oa1: the later of two dates` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `oa1: the later of two dates` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)

§ `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective`

-- Born March 1, 1950; received June 15, 2026; approved August 1, 2026. No earlier day prescribed: the day of approval.
#ASSERT `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) NOTHING EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1)
-- June 15, 2025 is allowed by s 8(2); June 15, 2026 by s 8(1) (and s 8(2)); June 14, 2025 by neither.
#ASSERT `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15)
#ASSERT `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15)
#ASSERT `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1950 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 6 14)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1)
-- A person under 65 when received (born 1962): s 8(1) alone applies.
#ASSERT `s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1962 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)

§ `s 8(1): the month in which payment commences`

-- "the first month after the application has been approved": a day in June gives July; a day in January gives February.
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 6 15) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 31) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1)
-- Where approval is effective as of an earlier day, the first month after approval is counted from that day (fork OA1-F18): received January 15, approved February 10,
-- earlier day January 15 (allowed by s 8(1)): the first month after January is February, not March.
#ASSERT `s 8(1): the month in which payment of the pension commences` (`s 8: the day as of which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 1960 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 15))) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)

§ `s 8(2.1): incarcerated at approval`

-- Approved while incarcerated, released June 20, 2026, notified: payment commences in respect of June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
-- "but only after they notify": no notice, no commencement. Not yet released: none.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` TRUE NOTHING TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not incarcerated at approval: s 8(1) governs.
#ASSERT `s 8(2.1): the month in respect of which payment of the pension commences` FALSE NOTHING FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1)

§ `s 8(3): duration`

-- Died March 20, 2026: the pension is paid for March, not April.
#ASSERT `s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20))
#ASSERT `s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20)))
#ASSERT `s 8(3): the pension is still paid for the month` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) NOTHING

§ `s 9(1) to (2): leaving Canada`

-- Left March 12, 2026, already a pensioner since January 2025: April to September are the six months (exclusive of March); October is suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) NOTHING
-- Returned in December 2026: payment resumes with the month of return, so November is suspended and December is not.
#ASSERT `s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 12 20))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 12 20)))
-- Left January 2026, before becoming a pensioner in May 2026: the six months count after becoming a pensioner (fork OA1-F8): June to November; December is suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 9(1): the pensioner has been absent from Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 1 12) (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) NOTHING
-- s 9(2): twenty years' residence when they left: no suspension.
#ASSERT `s 9(2): payment of the pension may be continued without suspension` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(2): payment of the pension may be continued without suspension` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 9(1) and (2): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because of absence` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1) and (2): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because of absence` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(1) and (2): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because of absence` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 9(3) to (4): ceasing to reside`

-- Ceased to reside in March 2026: six months after the end of March is the end of September; October is suspended.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) NOTHING
-- Resumed residence in December 2026: resumes with that month.
#ASSERT `s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 11 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 12 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3): the pensioner has ceased to reside in Canada and payment for the month falls to be suspended` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 31) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 12 5)))
-- s 9(4): twenty years' residence when they ceased to reside.
#ASSERT `s 9(3) and (4): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(3) and (4): payment of the pension for the month is suspended because the pensioner ceased to reside in Canada` TRUE TRUE)

§ `s 9(5): failure to comply`

-- "may be suspended": needs the failure and the Minister's decision, and ends when the pensioner has complied.
#ASSERT `s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9(5): payment of the pension is suspended for failure to comply` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 9.1: request that the pension cease, and reinstatement`

-- Approved March 12, 2026: ceases on March 31, 2026.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): the last day on which the pension is payable` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): the last day on which the pension is payable` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9.1(2): the last day on which the pension is payable` FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 12)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Reinstatement: only after a cessation, on written request.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(3): the pensioner may have the pension reinstated on request` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1(3): the pensioner may have the pension reinstated on request` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1(3): the pensioner may have the pension reinstated on request` TRUE FALSE)
-- Received April 10, 2026: the following month is May; a later chosen month (July) governs; an earlier one (March) does not.
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) NOTHING EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 7 15)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.1(4): the month in which payment of the reinstated pension commences` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 1)) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)
-- Ceased March 31, reinstated from May 1: March paid, April not, May paid. Never ceased: paid.
#ASSERT `s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 4 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1)))
#ASSERT `s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2026 5 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 31)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 9.1: the pension has not ceased to be payable for the month` (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) NOTHING NOTHING

§ `s 9.2: resumption after incarceration`

#ASSERT `s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` TRUE NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9.2: the month in respect of which payment of the pension resumes` FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 6 20)) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 9.3: request to cancel`

-- Payment commenced July 1, 2026; the time is six months (Regulations s 26.1(1)): the last day is January 1, 2027.
#ASSERT `s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1) (`a limit in months` 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 1 2) (`a limit in months` 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 30) (`a limit in months` 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the pension` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2026 8 1) (`a limit in months` 6))
-- Granted January 10, 2027, repaid by July 10, 2027 (six months after): deemed never made. A day later: not.
#ASSERT `s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 7 10)) (`a limit in months` 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 7 11)) (`a limit in months` 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) NOTHING (`a limit in months` 6))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 9.3(2): the application is deemed never to have been made and the pension is deemed not to have been payable` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 1 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 7 10)) (`a limit in months` 6))
